            <ArticleTitle>Pinhole balloon rupture during coronary angioplasty causing rupture of the coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of pinhole balloon rupture during percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty using one of the newer catheters. Pinhole balloon rupture resulted in rupture and occlusion of the vessel being dilated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
